## Build a Safe Banking System

### The Account Type with Invariant

```xiom
type Account = {
  owner: Str;
  balance: Float64;
}
  invariant: this.balance >= 0.0;
```

### Transfer with Full Contracts

```xiom
fn transfer(from: &mut Account, to: &mut Account, amount: Float64)
  requires: amount > 0.0;
  requires: amount <= from.balance;
  ensures: from.balance == from@pre.balance - amount;
  ensures: to.balance == to@pre.balance + amount;
{
  from.balance = from.balance - amount;
  to.balance = to.balance + amount;
}
```

### Read-Only Reporting

```xiom
fn report(account: &Account) {
  io.println(account.owner + ": $" + account.balance);
}

fn total_balance(accounts: &Vec[Account]) -> Float64 {
  let sum = 0.0;
  for a in accounts {
    sum = sum + a.balance;
  }
  return sum;
}
```

### Mutation with Safety

```xiom
fn deposit(account: &mut Account, amount: Float64)
  requires: amount > 0.0;
  ensures: account.balance == account@pre.balance + amount;
{
  account.balance = account.balance + amount;
}

fn withdraw(account: &mut Account, amount: Float64)
  requires: amount > 0.0;
  requires: amount <= account.balance;
  ensures: account.balance == account@pre.balance - amount;
{
  account.balance = account.balance - amount;
}
```

### All Together

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  var alice = Account{ owner: "Alice", balance: 1000.0 };
  var bob = Account{ owner: "Bob", balance: 500.0 };

  report(&alice);            // Read — no modification
  deposit(&mut bob, 200.0);  // Write — exclusive access
  transfer(&mut alice, &mut bob, 300.0);  // Two writes
  report(&alice);
  report(&bob);

  return alice.balance as Int;
}
```

